<!--
    kuna C-surface normalization: a statement of the shape `out = out OP y`
    (same high-level variable on both sides) renders as the C compound
    assignment `out OP= y` (user-reported readability issue on the angr fmt
    corpus binary: `v13 = v13 & v17;`; no upstream GH issue).

    Upstream Ghidra carries option_inplace_ops + the ten `OP=` tokens
    (printc.cc:62-71) but never consumed the flag; kuna ports the
    emitInplaceOp consumer and flips the default on (DIV-35,
    docs/history.md).  `option inplaceops off` restores the spelled-out
    form.  Comma contexts (for-loop headers) are exempt, so upstream
    `for (...; i = i + 1)` renders keep their shape.  A negative signed
    INT_ADD constant folds to subtraction: `x += -3` renders `x -= 3`.

    Stage model: S9 emission / statement-form policy.  P0 assertion:
    `option inplaceops on|off` (upstream OptionInPlaceOps).

    Three tiny loop functions, one self-op each (the loop-carried
    accumulator plus a store keeps the statement explicit; a trailing store
    keeps the tail from rerolling into a for-header, a comma context which
    inplaceops deliberately exempts):

    ca_add (0x100000):    mov eax,edi / jmp check /
                          body: add eax,esi ; x += y
                          mov [rdx],eax ; *p = x
                          check: cmp eax,0x63 / jle body / ret
    ca_and (0x100020):    same, body op and eax,esi ; x &= y
    ca_negadd (0x100040): mov eax,edi / jmp check /
                          body: add eax,-3 ; x -= 3 (negative-addend fold)
                          mov [rsi],eax ; *p = x
                          check: test eax,eax / jg body / ret

    Pass 1 (default): `+= y;` / `&= y;` / `-= 3;` each appear exactly once
    (asserts #1-#3) and the spelled-out forms do not.
    Pass 2 (option inplaceops off): the spelled-out ` + y;` / ` & y;` /
    ` + -3;` forms appear exactly once each (asserts #4-#6).
-->
